## 4. Policy and external demand (H3, H4)

Policy has to be read in two layers. **Realized impulse**, measured in credit and fiscal data, remains weak. {{ c("C-H3-01") }} {{ c("C-H3-02") }} {{ c("I-03") }} The **forward stance** has become more supportive: a late-September State Council executive meeting called for stronger counter-cyclical adjustment and a batch of incremental measures, and at the end of September the NDRC reported that the full year's consumer trade-in funding had been allocated. These are announcements and allocations, not yet realized impulse, and they were not part of the information in the frozen baseline judgment. They are listed with their official sources and stage in the policy context on the Evidence page.

